cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Preregistered research lab"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: DeAngelis
    given-names: Michael
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-02"
repository-code: "https://github.com/michaeldeangelis/preregistered-research-lab"
license: MIT
abstract: |
  A lab that tests a list of research questions without a person in the loop. Language-model
  workers check the literature, write a preregistered rule, write the analysis and review it; a
  plain Python kernel runs the code and decides each verdict from the rule, confirms passes on
  held-out units with a split key only it holds, and corrects for testing many questions at once.
  Workers and analyses run inside a macOS sandbox.
keywords:
  - research
  - preregistration
  - reproducibility
  - multiple-testing
  - agents
